WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Meet Shoal. Open-source Android apps for your content, your colours, and your choice.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.500
Sometimes, watching a video feels like an obstacle course: adverts, sponsorships, and
another upgrade prompt.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:22.500
A patched app can change the familiar experience. Morphe is one independent example. We
imagined a different habitat.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:29.500
Our fish adapt to their surroundings, and gather into a new home. Apps designed around
you.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:37.500
Swordfish brings SponsorBlock, background playback, picture in picture, and available
audio tracks to YouTube viewing.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:45.750
Clownfish brings Shorts, TikTok and Reels into separate tabs, with the services own
pages and account requirements.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:52.750
Pufferfish plays YouTube Music, with playlists, offline downloads, and lyrics when they
are available.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:59.750
Blobfish offers a Material You home for Bluesky, your feeds, conversations, and
community.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:07.500
Anglerfish wraps Reddit in a Material home. Reddit pages, sign-in requirements, and
restrictions still apply.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:15.500
Shoal installs and updates the family, and manages connected accounts. Silent
installation needs supported permissions or tools.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.500
Fish adapt to their surroundings and thrive in a natural habitat. That is the idea
behind Shoal.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:30.250
Shoal features have no paywalls. Donations are optional. Connected services may have
their own charges and restrictions.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:37.250
Built in the open. Shaped by the people who use it. By the community, for the community.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:44.250
Find your shoal at shoal apps, dot GitHub, dot I O. Everyone is welcome.
